me is $8$ cubic inches." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-be02a775-e3c8-5882-844e-a9ae15be7dd7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-be02a775-e3c8-5882-844e-a9ae15be7dd7" :answer-field/id #uuid "be02a775-e3c8-5882-844e-a9ae15be7dd7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4e964b86-655f-5b0f-90cf-94b1ab5e254d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8c00fcc4-4d8d-5ab0-be3c-4b4d04a0fdca" "answer-3f775cfe-b42f-568b-b1f0-6032ca161de1" "answer-d4af68cf-5c98-5792-99ee-4f578b8121f6" "answer-4e964b86-655f-5b0f-90cf-94b1ab5e254d" "answer-7323ec21-7cb0-5c3a-bfdb-8714016e43b9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8c00fcc4-4d8d-5ab0-be3c-4b4d04a0fdca" :answer/id #uuid "8c00fcc4-4d8d-5ab0-be3c-4b4d04a0fdca" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$5$ cubic inches" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3f775cfe-b42f-568b-b1f0-6032ca161de1" :answer/id #uuid "3f775cfe-b42f-568b-b1f0-6032ca161de1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$6$ cubic inches" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d4af68cf-5c98-5792-99ee-4f578b8121f6" :answer/id #uuid "d4af68cf-5c98-5792-99ee-4f578b8121f6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$7$ cubic inches" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e964b86-655f-5b0f-90cf-94b1ab5e254d" :answer/id #uuid "4e964b86-655f-5b0f-90cf-94b1ab5e254d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$8$ cubic inches" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7323ec21-7cb0-5c3a-bfdb-8714016e43b9" :answer/id #uuid "7323ec21-7cb0-5c3a-bfdb-8714016e43b9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$9$ cubic inches" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ff247414-d461-5a80-b3f1-dbef2f303fb7" :question/id #uuid "ff247414-d461-5a80-b3f1-dbef2f303fb7" :question/math-academy-id "q-58158" :question/problem "![](images/5f/5fd69cc862e1883c56b9266658ef8f08360bb2185dbf675e93e0820eac6b26e0.png)\n\nGiven that each cube represents $1$ cubic unit, find the volume of the figure." :question/worked-solution "The figure consists of $3$ cubes. \n\n![](images/7b/7b1b8c3d17177566d861ffcb2db4766a2175feb8b6d684598f1288ed8a6e0b0e.png)\n\nTherefore, its volume is $3$ cubic units." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-12365ab9-f192-59e1-a55f-90a90b9bdb9a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-12365ab9-f192-59e1-a55f-90a90b9bdb9a" :answer-field/id #uuid "12365ab9-f192-59e1-a55f-90a90b9bdb9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5f98707b-f416-5cc5-a441-922dca500c78" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5f98707b-f416-5cc5-a441-922dca500c78" "answer-2823e0d7-82d0-5160-81d6-a3e70a6a7fe9" "answer-d32432cc-49b4-5ad7-abdf-096ec5ba7fc4" "answer-7df5e380-d931-5fbd-926f-cf7b92e4d75e" "answer-683bc967-aee7-51ab-bf45-1d88e12ade15"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5f98707b-f416-5cc5-a441-922dca500c78" :answer/id #uuid "5f98707b-f416-5cc5-a441-922dca500c78" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$3$ cubic units" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2823e0d7-82d0-5160-81d6-a3e70a6a7fe9" :answer/id #uuid "2823e0d7-82d0-5160-81d6-a3e70a6a7fe9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$4$ cubic units" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d32432cc-49b4-5ad7-abdf-096ec5ba7fc4" :answer/id #uuid "d32432cc-49b4-5ad7-abdf-096ec5ba7fc4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$5$ cubic units" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7df5e380-d931-5fbd-926f-cf7b92e4d75e" :answer/id #uuid "7df5e380-d931-5fbd-926f-cf7b92e4d75e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$6$ cubic units" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-683bc967-aee7-51ab-bf45-1d88e12ade15" :answer/id #uuid "683bc967-aee7-51ab-bf45-1d88e12ade15" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$8$ cubic units" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186143995 :tutorial/content "**Volume** is the amount of space that an object takes up. We can measure volume with **unit cubes**, like the one below.\n\n![](images/a3/a318f6234bdbf014e4cbefbc1add274dbcc37b08f59d93a5fe53c463e962cc86.png)\n\nThese are called unit cubes because each one represents $1$ cubic unit. The volume of a figure is the number of unit cubes that make it up.\n\nFor example, let's find the volume of the figure below:\n\n![](images/12/1215ed078257410d4aab5cff0a58dcbc719c477211bdec8a77b9d10a2ecb5dae.png)\n\nThe figure consists of $2$ cubes. \n\n![](images/4b/4ba5e58d16c4bf9e684590e0280c4ddbd32c5b2c2bbf94412ca77713d9f059b0.png)\n\nTherefore, its volume is $2$ cubic units." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186143972 :tutorial/content "We can use metric and customary units to measure volume. \n\nConsider the cube below, whose length, width, and height all equal $1$ centimeter.\n\n![](images/2a/2a87c66750f85974528df85c7956a13a7e3a7982490d22113879ee80881badfb.png)\n\nSince the length, width, and height of this cube all equal $1$ centimeter,  the volume of this cube is $\\mathbf 1$ **cubic centimeter.**\n\nCommonly used metric units of volume are:\n\n- cubic meters\n\n- cubic centimeters\n\n- cubic millimeters\n\nCommonly used customary units of volume are:\n\n- cubic feet\n\n- cubic inches\n\nWe'll learn more about units of volume in future lessons." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186143996 :tutorial/content "If a figure has multiple layers, we can find its volume by first finding the volume of each layer and then adding the results.\n\nEach cube in the figure below represents one cubic unit. Let's find its volume.\n\n![](images/54/547a09fed5b5b736b556db4d476f869a68a39528f59d6a5abe505f1fa38260d9.png)\n\nThe figure consists of two layers:\n\n- The bottom layer consists of $2$ cubes.\n\n- The top layer consists of $2$ cubes, too.\n\n![](images/6b/6b7e4ce3ffa821b4263213782bf99a4243f3b844c862e49fcf5181a6f4cdacd2.png)\n\nTherefore, the volume is $2+2=4$ cubic units." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186143033 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
